The '''Myreque Hideouts''' are the safe-havens of the resistance force of the [[Myreque]], with each of them located in [[Morytania]]. They feature primarily in the Myreque quest chain, in which multiple different hideouts are used by the Myreque.

==Mort Myre==
The seven members of the Mort Myre Order of the [[Myreque]] are located underneath [[Mort Myre Swamp]], in a section of it named [[The Hollows]], called so because under the ground lies several large passages and alcove that serve as perfect locations for secretive operations. The Myreque have their first base located here. It is only accessible through a secret wall in the cellar of the [[Hair of the Dog]] tavern in [[Canifis]], or through a hollow tree, which is guarded by [[Curpile Fyod]], an affiliate of the Myreque. During [[In Search of the Myreque]], [[Vanstrom Klause]], the evil servant of [[Lord Drakan]], discovers the hideout and kills two members of the Myreque: [[Sani Piliu]] and [[Harold Evans]].

The passageway between [[Canifis]] and the [[Hollows]] contains several other cave entrances. The only other entrance on the eastern wall of the passageway, closer to Canifis, a [[werewolf]] town that the player first meets [[Vanstrom Klause]], is the entrance to the tomb of [[Ivandis Seergaze]], one of the fabled [[Seven Priestly Warriors]] who fell defending [[Misthalin]] from the onslaught of the [[Morytania]]ns, and blessing the [[River Salve]] in the process. The player must enter the tomb to create a replica of the [[rod of Ivandis]] that Seergaze used to fight the [[vampyre]]s. All other cave entrances in the passageway lead to small enclaves that contain creatures such as [[giant bat]]s, [[hobgoblin]]s and a multitude of [[rat]]s. After completion of [[In Search of the Myreque]] the player gains access to the {{Fairycode|DLS}} [[Fairy rings|Fairy ring]] located in a westernmost portion of the cave.
{{clear|left}}

==Burgh de Rott==
{{Map|name=Burgh de Rott|x=3502|y=3210|align=right|caption=After the unfortunate events at [[The Hollows]], the Myreque headed to [[Burgh de Rott]].}}
{{Map|3495,9628|mapID=-1|align=left|width=180|height=180|zoom=3|caption=The hideout under Burgh De Rott.}}
After the deaths of [[Sani Piliu|Sani]] and [[Harold Evans|Harold]] in the hideout situated in [[The Hollows]], the four surviving members of the [[Myreque]] ([[Veliaf Hurtz]], [[Polmafi Ferdygris]], [[Radigad Ponfit]] and [[Ivan Strom]]) move their base of operations to a large town in Southern [[Morytania]] called [[Burgh de Rott]]. The player helps by cleaning out rubble from an old cellar in a ruined and derelict inn to serve as a small war-room for the rebels. These events take place during the [[In Aid of the Myreque]] quest.

The integral position of Burgh de Rott, situated very close to the [[Sanguinesti region]] where [[Lowerniel Drakan]] himself resides, and the fact that the town of Burgh de Rott goes overlooked by [[Vanstrom]]'s [[Gadderanks|agents]] (who think it is deserted) make it a prime location for the Myreque to work from. The populace are trustworthy and helpful for their part, and the surviving members of the movement seem to like the town. It features heavily in the In Aid of the Myreque quest, and the following instalment in the series, [[Darkness of Hallowvale]], is started here in the inn basement when [[Veliaf]], the leader of the Mort Myre order, informs the player of the Sanguinesti order of the Myreque working in the capital city of [[Meiyerditch]].

After completion of [[The Blood Moon Rises]], the hideout is replaced with a [[brewery]], with [[Veliaf Hurtz]] operating a bar in the ruins of the building above it.
{{clear|left}}

==North Meiyerditch==
[[File:Darkness of Hallowvale map.png|thumb|right|In [[Darkness of Hallowvale]], the player discovered the Sanguinesti Myreque.]]
{{Map|align=left|mapID=-1|x=3628|y=9635|width=150|height=200|caption=The hideout under Meiyerditch.}}
The capital of [[Morytania]], a gigantic sprawling slum-city called [[Meiyerditch]], serves as a large ghetto for the [[vampyre]] overlords of the land. In the city, the populace are herded into four separate sectors to help keep order in the vampyric blood-farming that takes place in the [[Sanguinesti region]], and indeed all around Morytania (with the exception of the towns of [[Port Phasmatys]] and [[Mort'ton]], which are both dead and useless to the vampyres). [[Lord Drakan]] himself rules from this region, in his [[Castle Drakan|castle]] to the north of the city, in a section referred to as [[Darkmeyer]].

However, another group of the [[Myreque]], a militant group of well-organised rebels called the Sanguinesti Order, operate in this area, in a large underground barrack that is well-hidden and kitted out with useful supplies to the Myreque, such as [[silver sickle]]s, [[mithril bar]]s, [[silver bar]]s, [[papyrus]], and [[charcoal]].

In order to gain access to the Sanguinesti Hideout, the player must gain the help of a citizen of Meiyerditch, [[Old Man Ral]], who knows the lay of the city and tells the player about the entrance to the secret base. To enter, the player must slash a tapestry and push a secret lever in the form of a silver sickle, the symbol of the Myreque, to reveal a secret trapdoor in the floor leading to the base. Near the end of [[Darkness of Hallowvale]], shortcut doors are unlocked along the path to the hideout. [[File:Meiyerditch Shortcut Door Section 1.png|thumb|Building with the shortcut door in section 1 of Meiyerditch]]
[[File:Meiyerditch Shortcut Door Section 2.png|thumb|Building with the shortcut door in sector 2 of Meiyerditch|302x302px]]

During [[A Taste of Hope]], the northern Meiyerditch Hideout becomes compromised after the [[Abomination]] successfully tracks down the Sanguinesti order, killing [[Mekritus A'hara]], [[Andiess Juip]], and [[Flaygian Screwte]]. Interacting with the [[decorated wall]] after defeating the Abomination will result in the player commenting that it is too dangerous to stick around. This still occurs even after completing [[The Blood Moon Rises]].
{{clear|left}}

==South Meiyerditch==
After the [[Abomination]] is defeated during [[A Taste of Hope]], a new hideout in the southern part of Meiyerditch can be accessed through a [[Trapdoor (Old Man Ral's house)|trapdoor]] in [[Old Man Ral]]’s house. Once unlocked, the old northern hideout becomes inaccessible, and the southern hideout becomes the Myreque's main base.

The hideout is used as the main base of all the surviving Myreque during [[Sins of the Father]]. Only [[Ivan Strom]] remains in the hideout after the quest, as [[Veliaf Hurtz]] has left, [[Safalaan Hallow]] has been captured, and all other Myreque members have been killed by [[Lowerniel Drakan]].

During [[The Blood Moon Rises]], the hideout is abandoned after the player recruits Ivan to try and help save Safalaan.

